  "body": "Add the GUI workflow in `crates/ui` to open external NC files and play back stock removal.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `File -> Open G-code...` (`.nc`, `.tap`, `.gcode`, `.i`) with a dialect selector tied to the mounted machine or built-in post.\n- Prompt the user to assign any unmapped `T<n>` tool number to a document tool, catalog tool, or `.camtools` library before running simulation.\n- Show setup inputs (stock, target model, fixtures, WCS origin) and report missing stock or unjudged target status clearly.\n- Feed the `PlaySeed` from #2218 into `PlayWorker` (`crates/app/src/stock_play_worker.rs`) and `FieldPlay` (`crates/app/src/stock_play.rs`) for playback and Deviate coloring.\n- Load the NC text and line map into `gcode_view` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/gcode_view.rs`) so `gcode_segment` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs`) highlights the active move and jumps to line findings.\n\nDepends on #2218.\n\nDone means: Structural and `egui_kittest` UI tests open an NC fixture, bind an unmapped `T` number, run `PlayWorker` playback and Deviate, and highlight the active NC line segment via `gcode_segment`.\n\nPart of #2213\n",
